      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A 1912 wooden church and an 1857 cemetery are two of Petrolia's oldest surviving landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://secretsanfrancisco.com/petrolia-california-lost-coast/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Mattole River hosts over 250 bird species and the threatened Mattole salmon, a focus of a two‑decade preservation effort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petrolia%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nestled on the Lost Coast, Petrolia borders one of the longest undeveloped U.S. coastlines and stands amid virgin old‑growth Douglas fir.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petrolia%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Only two roads reach Petrolia: one from Ferndale north, one from Honeydew south, both winding through redwood forests filmed for Jurassic Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
